    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the throughput logs aren't showing a corresponding traffic spike, then you are right to start suspecting something more subtle than simple congestion. Intermittent electrical issues, like marginal power supplies or failing line cards, can absolutely cause these brief, sporadic bursts of errors that manifest as packet loss. These hardware glitches are often the hardest to track down because they are so fleeting, making them look like a phantom problem. I'd suggest checking the SNMP interface statistics on the routers around hops 4 and 5 for CRC errors or input/output errors.",
      "source": "target",
